#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""phonecam — phone camera and Lovense overlay for OBS.

Phone side: generates a VDO.Ninja room, puts it into an OBS browser source and
shows a QR code that the phone scans to start publishing.

Lovense side: runs a local relay that speaks the Lovense OBS Toolset protocol,
serves the Lovense Cam widget to OBS and answers the Lovense Chrome extension.
No Splitcam, no Windows toolset, no virtual camera drivers.

Usage:
  phonecam start                  start the relay, create OBS sources, show QR
  phonecam doctor                 check the environment
  phonecam phone <command>        phone camera commands
  phonecam lovense <command>      Lovense widget commands

Shorthand aliases (kept for compatibility):
  new, url, qr, obs, all, refresh, layout, status, enable-ws

Ports (must match the Lovense extension and widget):
  20996  the Chrome extension always dials ws://localhost:20996
  11000  internal relay (the widget reads ?port=, default 11000)
  8888   HTTP server that serves the widget and /health
"""

